OL,3,GNEWSATop GCSE results in Wales see
OL,4,Aslight increase after major changes to
OL,5,Aqualifications
OL,6,
OL,7,FTop GCSE grades in Wales have risen
OL,8,Fslightly following major changes to
OL,9,Fqualifications in the country, but the
OL,10,Foverall pass rate was slightly down.
OL,12,FThe proportion of top A* and A grades
OL,13,Fwas up 0.1% to 19.6%, while 62.3%
OL,14,Freceived grades at C or above, a drop
OL,15,Fof 0.2%.
OL,17,FThe proportion of pupils who received a
OL,18,Fpassing grade was 96.8%, a drop of
OL,19,F0.1%.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
